{
  "id": "investigatory-behavior",
  "term": "investigatory behavior",
  "definition": "Investigatory behavior is exploratory responding toward a stimulus used to assess how an animal evaluates it, especially in social tests. In the supplied source, it refers mainly to a mouse’s distance-based investigation of social stimuli, shaped in sequence by checking novelty through smell and then by tactile social contact.",
